=== THM-469 core (the bi-dyadic seam): v_p level-sets SUM-FREE ⟺ p=2 ===
  p= 2: ALL levels SUM-FREE ✓
  p= 3: FAILS: v_3-level 0 has 1+1=2 ✗
  p= 5: FAILS: v_5-level 0 has 1+1=2 ✗
  p= 7: FAILS: v_7-level 0 has 1+1=2 ✗
  p=11: FAILS: v_11-level 0 has 1+1=2 ✗
  p=13: FAILS: v_13-level 0 has 1+1=2 ✗
  ⟹ p=2 unique ⟹ the obstruction grading is BINARY ⟹ the tree-grid 'grid' is the 2^n BINARY subgrid.

=== the three axes (state of the art, cross-checked vs the repo + literature) ===
  n-axis  R(n,2): n=1→3, n=2→5, n=3→7? ; 2n+1 = [3, 5, 7, 9, 11]  (HYP-2396; tame/LINEAR)
  m-axis  ω^(ω^m): m=1 YES Chang'72 | m=2 YES Schipperus | m=3 OPEN $1000 | m≥4 NO Schipperus  (WILD/tower)
  b-axis  binary subgrid b=2 (the universal obstruction-atom); R_b(1)=R(3,b) (THM-464)

=== the new framing: PRE-TOWER (n) vs TOWER (m), bridged by the binary atom ===
  ω^n  (finite CNF exponent, n<ω): BELOW the first limit exponent → no tower → R(n,2) LINEAR (2n+1).
  ω^(ω^m) (CNF exponent ω^m, crosses the limit ω): the TOWER regime; Chang (m=1) is its base;
          the open m=3 stacks THREE binary-subgrid-tower levels (THM-460 B3 shape grammar).
  The binary subgrid (b=2) is the obstruction-ATOM at EVERY rank (THM-460 B3: pairs at e=0,
          M-towers at limit scales) — carried across the limit by the p=2 sum-free seam.
